{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf6RVtnh8NX2A5jicDAbT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have analyzed the codebase. Let me summarize my findings:\n\n**Repository findings (cited as path:line):**\n- Order entity without status: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/Order.kt:11-16`\n- OrderController: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/OrderController.kt:22-34`\n- OrderRepository: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/OrderRepository.kt:11-27`\n- Shipment entity with status: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:9-27`\n- ShipmentController: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt:26-43`\n- ShipmentRepository: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt:11-26`\n- Error handling patterns: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiExceptions.kt`\n- ErrorCode enum: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt:31-37`\n\n**Conventions:**\n1. Errors use sealed ApiException with ResourceNotFoundException (404) and ConflictException (409)\n2. ErrorCode enum is the single source of error codes (currently has ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED)\n3. Controllers use @PostMapping, @GetMapping, @PathVariable annotations from Spring Web\n4. In-memory repository pattern with ConcurrentHashMap (no database)\n5. Tests use @SpringBootTest, @AutoConfigureMockMvc with MockMvc and jsonPath assertions\n6. Error responses have stable shape with error.code and error.message fields\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `Order.kt` - Add status field with enum (ACTIVE/CANCELLED)\n2. `OrderRepository.kt` - Add method to find shipments by orderId\n3. `OrderController.kt` - Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint\n4. `ShipmentRepository.kt` - Add method to find all shipments for an order\n5. `ShipmentController.kt` - Add validation to prevent shipment creation for cancelled orders\n6. `ApiError.kt` - Add error codes for cancel operation conflicts\n7. `OrderControllerTest.kt` - Add tests for cancel endpoint\n8. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` - Add test for rejected shipment creation on cancelled order\n\n**Risks:**\n1. The Order data class needs the status field; existing code creating Order instances may fail\n2. Idempotency requirement means cancel must work correctly when called multiple times\n3. All-or-nothing semantics requires careful transaction handling (though we're in-memory)\n4. Need to find all shipments for an order to check for CONFIRMED status before cancelling\n\n**Open questions:** None - the ticket clearly defines all cases.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** - Add OrderStatus enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) and a status field to the Order data class. New orders default to ACTIVE.\n\n2. **OrderRepository.kt** - Keep as-is; we'll access shipments via ShipmentRepository (injected in OrderController).\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** - Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method to find all shipments for a given order.\n\n4. **OrderController.kt** - Add `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that:\n   - Finds the order (404 if not found via ResourceNotFoundException)\n   - If order is already CANCELLED, return it unchanged (idempotent)\n   - Check if any shipment is CONFIRMED (409 with ConflictException if so, no changes made)\n   - Otherwise, set order status to CANCELLED and cancel all CREATED shipments\n   - Return the cancelled order with 200 OK\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt** - In the `create` method, add a check: if the order doesn't exist, current behavior (create shipment); if the order is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with 409.\n\n6. **ApiError.kt** - Add ErrorCode values:\n   - `ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENTS` - for cancel rejected due to confirmed shipments\n   - `ORDER_IS_CANCELLED` - for shipment creation rejected on cancelled order\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt** - Add tests:\n   - Cancel an ACTIVE order succeeds and returns CANCELLED status\n   - Repeated cancel on CANCELLED order succeeds (idempotent)\n   - Cancel with CONFIRMED shipment returns 409 and changes nothing\n   - Cancel non-existent order returns 404\n\n8. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Add test:\n   - Create shipment for CANCELLED order returns 409\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Using a service layer (OrderService) vs. putting logic in controller: Rejected because the existing code doesn't use services, only controllers + repositories. Staying consistent with the codebase pattern.\n- Adding CONFIRMATION status transition to Order: Rejected because the requirement only mentions cancellation, not confirmation.\n- Using database transactions: Not applicable; we're using in-memory storage, and ConcurrentHashMap operations are atomic enough for this use case.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n1. **Cancel existing ACTIVE order:**\n   - Read: Order with status=ACTIVE, find all shipments with that orderId\n   - Check: Any shipment with status=CONFIRMED? If yes → return 409 ConflictException, nothing changes\n   - Write: Set order.status = CANCELLED, set all shipments with status=CREATED to status=CANCELLED\n   - Return: 200 OK with updated Order\n\n2. **Cancel already-CANCELLED order:**\n   - Read: Order with status=CANCELLED\n   - Write: Nothing\n   - Return: 200 OK with the order unchanged (idempotent)\n\n3. **Cancel non-existent order:**\n   - Read: Order not found\n   - Return: 404 ResourceNotFoundException\n\n4. **Create shipment for CANCELLED order:**\n   - Read: Order with status=CANCELLED\n   - Return: 409 ConflictException ORDER_IS_CANCELLED, no shipment created\n\n5. **Create shipment for non-existent order:**\n   - Current behavior: Create the shipment (order may not exist yet)\n   - New behavior: Same as current (no change to this path)\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\nOrderControllerTest additions:\n- Test 1: Cancel ACTIVE order → 200 OK, order.status=CANCELLED, order returned\n- Test 2: Cancel CANCELLED order again → 200 OK, no changes, order returned (idempotency)\n- Test 3: Cancel order with CONFIRMED shipment → 409 ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENTS, order stays ACTIVE, shipments unchanged\n- Test 4: Cancel non-existent order → 404 ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n- Test 5: Cancel ACTIVE order cancels all CREATED shipments → verify they're in CANCELLED status\n\nShipmentControllerTest additions:\n- Test 1: Create shipment for CANCELLED order → 409 ORDER_IS_CANCELLED\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nLet me start implementing the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":21386,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7d075699-a072-4454-b7d8-48dd085fdf4b","uuid":"af8f1d52-9abc-46b1-81ce-4ad8f6d699f2","timestamp":"2026-09-16T03:39:59.619Z","request_id":"req_011Cf6RVtVposWUNNbrh2rMd"}
